  "body": "As far as I can tell, there is no special handling of the `height` attribute on `<tbody>`, `<thead>`, or `<tfoot>`.  But in browsers it's mapped into style.  Testcase:\r\n```\r\n<table style=\"border: 1px solid red\">\r\n  <thead style=\"display: block\" height=\"100\">\r\n    <tr>\r\n      <td>\r\n        thead text\r\n      </td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</table>\r\n```\r\nChrome and Safari don't seem to change the height if the display of the `<thead>` is `display: table-header-group`, but they ignore the CSS `height` property in that case too.  So they are in fact mapping the attribute to style, but then ignoring the style.\r\n\r\nWe should probably spec the mapping behavior here.  0 _does_ get mapped to style in all browsers here.\r\n\r\n@annevk ",
